      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The main understandability issues are: repeated `result` reassignment without context, verbose `SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, ...)` calls throughout, and no indication of what each scenario tests.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The error is a generic type mismatch in the `input` helper method. I'll fix it with an unchecked cast so the return type matches the caller's `E`.The test compiles successfully. The improved version extracts a typed `input()` helper to eliminate repeated `SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, …)` boilerplate, adds an `assertResult()` helper to consolidate the four per-case assertions into a single readable call, and adds a brief comment above each scenario describing the edit operation being tested (empty-to-empty, insertion, deletion, substitution, mixed)."
    }
